// Mentor overview: target workflow, not an implemented emergency service.
title Avertiq - the simple plan
direction right
colorMode pastel
styleMode plain
typeface clean
textSize medium

Report [label: "1. REPORT\nTruck or storage\nincident", color: orange]
Inputs [label: "2. COLLECT\nChemical + tank + weather\nSave input revision", color: blue]
Check [shape: diamond, label: "3. CHECK\nEnough evidence?\nMethod supported?", color: orange]
Missing [label: "EXPLAIN THE GAP\nAsk for missing facts\nDo not invent a result", color: red]
Assess [label: "4. ASSESS\nIllustrative demo today\nQualified physics later", color: purple]
Map [label: "5. EXPLAIN ON MAP\nShow zone + meaning\nFlag nearby places", color: green]
Review [label: "6. AUTHORITY REVIEW\nVerify evidence\nDecide response", color: green]
Share [label: "7. HANDOVER\nRecord decisions\nOnly approved public notices", color: green]

Report > Inputs
Inputs > Check
Check > Missing: No
Check > Assess: Yes
Assess > Map
Map > Review
Review > Share

// Steps 2-7 describe the target process. Current incident state is browser-local.
// New evidence restarts at step 2 with a new revision; the old result becomes stale.
// Demo zones are illustrative, not calculated. A failed run produces a reason, not a zone.
// No automatic evacuation or safe-route judgement. 3D terrain is visual context only.
